 ### Comparison with Rossignac and Borrel Grading
-Rossignac and Borrel's original method grades vertices by the longest incident edge length and the maximum angle between incident edges. This method replaces those with the maximum area of incident faces. The change is necessary because edge-angle metrics are unreliable for pre-triangulated datasets, which are common in volume rendering contexts [S1, unofficial].
