 ### Comparison with Lindstrom's Algorithm
-This method is chosen over Lindstrom's algorithm [81, 84] because vertex clustering is simpler, faster, and requires only a single data traversal, which is critical for I/O-bound systems. It also produces bounded Hausdorff error and does not require maintaining topological adjacency graphs [S1, unofficial].
